{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe upward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 3-5 EUR when the true market exhibits high volatility or mean reversion, regardless of neutral sentiment.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after spikes: When true prices spike (e.g., >75 EUR), the model fails to anticipate the subsequent sharp drop; apply a -2 to -4 EUR correction in the 5-10 day horizon following any peak above 74 EUR.",
    "Ignore lagging sentiment signals: Positive sentiment scores (1.00) in the history do not correlate with sustained price increases; treat high sentiment as a potential contrarian signal for a short-term pullback rather than a buy signal.",
    "Adjust for horizon-specific decay: The model's linear upward drift is invalid beyond day 5; flatten the forecast slope to zero or slightly negative after the first week to align with the observed cyclical nature of the data.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude during volatility: When the 18-day history shows a range exceeding 8 EUR (indicating regime change), reduce the forecasted price level by 2.5% to account for the model's inability to capture sudden structural breaks."
  ]
}
